# =============================================================================
# infrastructure — .gitignore
# =============================================================================
# This repo tracks the SELF-AUTHORED tools that exist nowhere else. Anything
# that is already a git repo with its own remote is EXCLUDED and documented in
# README.md ("clone these here") — one source of truth each, no nested repos.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- separately-versioned repos (see README.md for remotes) ------------------
tools/ticket-panel/
tools/claude-hooks/
tools/mcp-d2-diagrams/
tools/mcp-markdown-to-pdf/
tools/mcp-trello/
tools/mcp-google-workspace/

# --- abandoned upstream clones (recoverable from upstream if ever wanted) ----
tools/_archive/

# --- dependencies & caches (regenerate) --------------------------------------
node_modules/
.venv/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
*.pyc

# --- secrets safety net ------------------------------------------------------
# Carry the shape, never the value. Note: patterns cover BOTH `foo.env` and
# files literally named `env` or `.env*` (the dev-environment repo's audit
# found `*.env` alone misses the latter — don't repeat that hole here).
*.env
.env
.env.*
env
!*.env.example
!*.env.template
!.env.example
!.env.template
*.pem
*.key
id_*
**/.credentials.json
**/hosts.yml
token
